<netpdl name="NetPDL custom protocol" description="ASK2 G4 dispatch probe: ESP to a KeyGen scheme by NIA">
<!--
  G4 multi-table dispatch probe (plans/ASK2-MASTER-PLAN.md G4, 2026-11-09).
  On the IPsec HXS (slot 12, AH and ESP) the routine writes the KeyGen-direct
  NIA for one scheme and ends the parse: NIA_ENG_HWK 0x480000 | AC_CC 0x200 |
  KG_DIRECT 0x100 | scheme id (0x14 = 20 here). KeyGen then runs that scheme
  without the match-vector walk, so the port's routed scheme (lower id, mv 0)
  keeps every other frame. Compile (vendor fmc, host build, see
  specs/ask2-soft-parser-lcv-scheme-select.md 6s):
    fmc -d etc/fmc/config/hxs_pdl_v3.xml -s g4_esp_dispatch.xml --sp_only -t 0x80
  Result: 4 words, position independent:
    0x095F0314 0x00480001 0x1BFF0001 0x1BFE0000
  Attach: pmda[12].ssa = (old & ~0x7FF) | 0x400 | label.
-->
<protocol name="espschema" longname="espschema" prevproto="ipsec_esp">
    <execute-code>
      <before>
        <assign-variable name="$nia" value="0x480314"/>
        <action type="exit" confirm="yes" nextproto="end_parse"/>
      </before>
    </execute-code>
  </protocol>
</netpdl>
